<h3>Formula Sheet Protocol</h3>
<ul>
<li>Maintain <strong>3 separate formula books</strong> (Physics, Chemistry, Maths).</li>
<li>Write formulas in your own handwriting—no copy-paste.</li>
<li>Add one-line context for each formula: &quot;When is this used? What is the unit?&quot;</li>
<li>Review formula books every Sunday (30 minutes minimum).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Concept Map Strategy</h3>
<ul>
<li>For each chapter, create a <strong>single A4 page concept map</strong> within 24 hours of completing it.</li>
<li>Include: Main concept → sub-concepts → key formulas → common mistake points.</li>
<li>Use color coding: Red for frequently forgotten, Yellow for moderate, Green for solid.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Monthly Integration</h3>
<ul>
<li>At the end of every month, solve <strong>one full-syllabus chapter-mix test</strong> mixing questions from all chapters covered so far.</li>
<li>This forces cross-topic recall and reveals integration gaps.</li>
</ul>
